Ansible Inventory:
-----------------
Ansible can work with one or multiple systems.
Agentless - No need to install any additonal software on the target machines to be able to work with ansible.
Information about target machines stored in an inventory file.
If we will not create any new inventory file ansible uses default inventory file located in /etc/ansible/hosts locations

Single Inventory file:
----------------------
server1.company.com
server2.company.com
[mail]
server1.company.com
server1.company.com
[db]
server1.company.com
server1.company.com
[web]
server1.company.com
server1.company.com

More on Inventory Files:
------------------------
Inventory Parameters:
--------------------
web  ansible_host=server1.company.com ansible_connection=ssh ansible_user=root
db   ansible_host=server2.company.com ansible_connection=winrm
mail ansible_host=server3.company.com
web2 ansible_host=server4.company.com
ansible_host inventory parameter is used to specify the FQDN or IPA ddress of the server.

localhost ansible_connection = localhost

ansible_connection - ssh/winrm/localhost
ansible_user - 22/9856
ansible_port - root/administartor
ansible_ssh_pass - Password

Why do we need different inventory formats?
-------------------------------------------
Start-up Company -> FewServers -> [web hosting & Database management]

Different types of Inventory Format Types:
------------------------------------------
INI & YAML

INI Format:
----------
[webservers]
web1.example.com
web2.example.com

[dbservers]
db1.example.com
db2.example.com

YAML Format:
-----------
all:
  children:
    webservers:
      hosts:
        web1.example.com
        web2.example.com
    dbservers:
      hosts:
        db1.example.com
        db2.example.com

Grouping and Parent Child RelationShips Examples [INI]
------------------------------------------------------
[webservers:children]
webservers_us
webservers_eu

[webservers_us]
server1_us.com  ansible_host=192.168.8.101
server2_us.com  ansible_host=192.168.8.102

[webserver_eu]
server1_eu.com  ansible_host=192.168.8.101
server2_eu.com  ansible_host=192.168.8.102

Grouping and Parent Child RelationShips Examples [YAML]
-------------------------------------------------------
all:
  children:
    webserver:
      children:
        webserver_us:
          hosts:
            server1_us.com:
              ansible_hosts: 192.168.20.1
            server2_us.com:
              ansible_hosts: 192.168.20.1
        webserver_eu
          hosts:
            server1_eu.com:
              ansible_hosts:192.68.21.1
            server2_eu.com:
              ansible_hosts:192.168.12.1

Ansible Variables:
-----------------
Example is Patches 100 of servers at a time

Variables Types:
---------------
(1)String Variables
(2)Number Variables

(1)String Variables:
--------------------
(1)String variables in ansible are sequences of characters
They can be defined in a playbook,inventory or passed as a command line arguments
[username: "admin"]
(2)Number Variables:
Number Variables can hold integer or floating point values.
[max_connections: 100]
(3)Boolean Variables: true or false
[debug_mode: true]
(4)List Variables: List variables in Ansible can hold an ordered collection of values.
packages:
  - nginx
  - postgresql
  - git
(5)Dictionary Variables: It can hold a collection of key-value pairs.
user:
  name: "admin"
  password: "secret"
